course: dictionary
lesson: 4385
title: A fish called haddock
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A haddock is a fish that lives in the sea of the North Atlantic, near the sea floor. It is related to cod, a fish many people know from fish and chips.
explain: Look for the clues in the description: a haddock has a black line along its side and a dark spot near its fins. «Fish fingers are usually white fish such as cod, pollock or haddock.» The list tells you haddock is one of several similar fish.
explain: Use the list as a clue. Cod, pollock and haddock are all named together, so haddock must be a fish. Check your idea by putting «fish» in the sentence in place of haddock. If it still makes sense, you are right.
fact: A haddock is a sea fish of the North Atlantic.
fact: Haddock is related to cod, and it is a popular food fish.
fact: A haddock has a black line along its side and a dark spot near its fins.
fact: «Fish fingers are usually white fish such as cod, pollock or haddock, cut into blocks and breadcrumbed, and were first sold in Britain in 1955.»
fact: In Scotland, smoked haddock is called finnan haddie. Haddock often eats small animals that live near the sea floor.
exercise: What kind of animal is a haddock? | A kind of seaweed | A bird that lives on cliffs | *A sea fish | A small mammal from the forest
exercise: Which fish is haddock related to? | Tuna | Shark | *Cod | Salmon
exercise: Which clue helps you spot a haddock in the sea? | *A black line along its side | It has a long, furry tail | It can fly over the water | It has bright red feathers
test: In «white fish such as cod, pollock or haddock», what kind of thing is haddock? | A kind of ship | *A kind of fish | A kind of sauce | A kind of bread
test: Overfishing has made fishing limits necessary. What does overfishing mean? | Fishing in a river instead of the sea | Eating fish for breakfast | Cooking fish for much too long | *Catching so many fish that too few are left
exam: Which sentence uses haddock correctly? | The haddock flew over the hill | The haddock rang the loud bell | We walked the haddock to school | *Smoked haddock is often eaten for breakfast
